WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.260
- [Interviewer] Alright, Ann.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.290
Welcome back.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.123
- Hi.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.470
- [Interviewer] So the
last time you were here

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.180
you told me about what happened to you.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.910
Was that on Figueroa?

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:15.398
- No, well, I left from Figueroa,

00:00:15.398 --> 00:00:17.070
but it didn't happen on Figueroa.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.410
- [Interviewer] You're on another street

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.340
or were you even on the street?

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.540
- I was looking to another
street, I told you,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.433
I left with a friend that I trusted.

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:27.700
- [Interviewer] You got
beaten up and all kinds

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.660
of crazy stuff for like three days.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.767
- Yes, that, well, I left
with a friend from Figueroa,

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.530
and we ended up somewhere else.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.770
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
it's a horrible story.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.270
So what's going on in your
life since, since then?

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:42.270
- I'm just taking it one day at a time

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.670
and I'm trying to catch
up with everything.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.290
I finally caught up with my rent for

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.360
as my living situation.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.965
So now, you know, instead of
owing them, so many hundreds,

00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:54.810
I'm back to pay at $80 a day

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.920
which is hard because it's like,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.970
once you pay the 80 dollars,

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:03.023
you only get a few hours out of a day.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.100
If you relax and then you

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.990
you have to be right back
out there to do it again,

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.410
and again, and again,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.520
And it's really, it takes a
toll on you, it really does.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.742
- [Interviewer] So are you still working?

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:17.580
- Yes.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.413
- [Interviewer] The same way you were?

00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:19.820
- I have no choice.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.850
- [Interviewer] You have no choice.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.340
- I have to.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.070
I mean I don't want to be homeless

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.010
in the streets, you know,
or nothing like that.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:30.310
You know, I'm still trying
to build everything back up.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.810
Everything is still
pretty, basically hard.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.833
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.830
It's like

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.150
you succeed one day

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.640
and you get like maybe, maybe an hour,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.440
maybe two to feel good because
you did this or whatever.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.470
But in reality, you're
just, it's never ending.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.810
It's never ending because
you got me every single day.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.720
You have to deal with this.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.223
You know, a lot of times lately
I've been sleeping a lot.

00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:08.900
I've been sleeping a lot.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.870
It's like I do what I
have to do to survive

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.180
but I just, you know, I'm tired.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.238
- [Interviewer] But you're living,

00:02:16.238 --> 00:02:18.180
like, it sounds like day by day?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.760
- Day by day, hour by
hour, minute by minute,

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.093
second by second.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.631
It's like being in the middle

00:02:28.631 --> 00:02:32.040
of the ocean and you try to
swim to the shore to get out,

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.770
but these waves are
steady pushing you back

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.130
and you're not able to get to
that shore, you right there,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:38.963
but you get this wave.

00:02:38.963 --> 00:02:41.420
It's going to push you back so many feet

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.253
and then you got to swim harder

00:02:42.253 --> 00:02:44.370
and harder and harder to try to make it.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.340
And you're so tired, you know,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.160
you feel like it's just going to end.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:48.993
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:48.993 --> 00:02:50.820
It's just, that's how it feels.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.400
You know, basically that's how it is.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.460
- [Interviewer] And has it
been harder to do this kind

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.210
of work since what happened to you?

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.780
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.613
You know I have to pray a lot

00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:04.700
and I have to just hold my
head up and it was like, okay,

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.827
we're going to get through
this day who want to do this?

00:03:06.827 --> 00:03:07.910
And you know what I'm saying?

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.220
It's like, but I'm
paranoid all the time now.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.420
I'm very much afraid

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.420
because it's like every car that I get in,

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.090
it's like, is this person
going to try to hurt me?

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.610
Is this person going to
try to do something to me?

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.800
You know, it's really, really scary now,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:26.633
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:26.633 --> 00:03:30.170
But I still got to do what
I gotta do to survive.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.263
You know, you know, it was kinda,

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:37.330
Only thing I did different this time.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.580
Okay I talked to a friend
of mine and she works also.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:44.230
So she told me about
a school and it's UEI.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.020
You know, because I had went to school,

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.160
I wanted to go to school,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.070
maybe Jack will help change
and everything like that

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.610
I did the whole application

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.950
everything talked to people online.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.230
And then we got to the financial aid part.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:59.540
They said that my student loans and stuff.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.830
So all of a sudden, everything
just stopped right there.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.633
And it oh, well, if you get this,

00:04:06.633 --> 00:04:09.550
once you get this part taken care

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.833
of everything like
that, they call me back.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.060
They just cut my whole application off.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.570
And that right there
just took a toll on me

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.793
because it was like,
wow, for real, you know.

00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:27.927
So I've been kinda I would say

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:34.710
doubtful now because I
tried to take another turn,

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.850
do something positive,

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.960
and I got shut down on that.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.620
So it's like, I feel like,
you know, none of them,

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.930
I just had a birthday

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.177
and everything is just, it's just life.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.480
I fucked up life.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.052
- [Interviewer] Yeah, hope is
an important thing to have.

00:04:56.052 --> 00:04:57.584
And you get that kind of, yeah.

00:04:57.584 --> 00:04:59.660
- I tried to tell myself
okay you can do something

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.460
about this situation
with the financial aid.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.570
Maybe you could still go to school.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.410
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:09.330
And it seem to me everything
in his world revolve

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.410
around money, money, money, money,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.630
and materialistic things.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.020
And that just really fucks me up.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:14.933
It bothers me.

00:05:15.811 --> 00:05:18.140
It really does because it's like

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.158
no matter what you're doing, you know,

00:05:19.158 --> 00:05:22.690
more money you see the
more problems you have

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:23.523
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.520
You can't get forward.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.250
That's why so many girls we can't get out

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:29.220
of this situation because we
got everyday things going on.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.560
You know if you're trying to live a life

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.400
and you have no other choice,
you know, what can you do?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.950
- [Interviewer] There are
less expensive places to live

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.783
in California.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:43.470
- No, no, I, the lesson, the
lesson, I don't see that.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.860
- [Interviewer] You're from Texas, right?

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.423
- Yeah.

00:05:48.423 --> 00:05:50.830
- [Interviewer] Moving back
to Texas must be cheaper.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.663
- I can't.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.440
And I'm embarrassed to say,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.060
but I got kicked out of the state of Texas

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:57.893
when I was younger.

00:05:57.893 --> 00:05:59.481
So I can't go back to Texas.

00:05:59.481 --> 00:06:02.730
- [Interviewer] You can't go back?

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.730
- No so it's like where I stay right now,

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:08.980
I'm really comfortable.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:10.863
You know?

00:06:10.863 --> 00:06:11.696
'Cause when I'm inside my place,

00:06:11.696 --> 00:06:14.550
I'm in my own world and I
don't really realize where

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.030
I'm at unless I open my door

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:20.840
and go outside that it's
like, you know, it's like--

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.180
- [Interviewer] Is it a new
place or the same place?

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.140
- The same place.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.107
- [Interviewer] Oh you got
it back because it sounded

00:06:24.107 --> 00:06:25.910
like they were kicking
you out or something.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.340
- Well, yeah, they kept locking me out.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.810
I've been locked out so many times

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.530
I think that's what made me
stronger because you know

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.053
like I said, when I got
back lock on, you know,

00:06:34.926 --> 00:06:35.759
lock on my door and everything

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:40.250
like that and it's like,
oh my God, this is crazy.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.083
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:41.083 --> 00:06:43.830
And as much as I try to give him this,

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.570
try and give him that, and I'm still in,

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.460
then at the end of the day
they say I still get locked

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.861
out because I don't want, you know--

00:06:48.861 --> 00:06:51.508
- [Interviewer] You got some
nice help from my viewers,

00:06:51.508 --> 00:06:52.584
right?

00:06:52.584 --> 00:06:54.030
You got some nice help from my viewers?

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:54.863
- Oh my God.

00:06:54.863 --> 00:06:55.703
I'm totally shocked.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.491
Totally shocked right now.

00:06:58.491 --> 00:06:59.324
- [Interviewer] I think a lot of females

00:06:59.324 --> 00:07:00.600
really related to your story.

00:07:01.544 --> 00:07:05.900
- That makes me feel
good and I'm a cry baby.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:06.733
Excuse me.

00:07:06.733 --> 00:07:11.640
But I want to thank everybody
for caring and donation

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.150
whatever I totally didn't
expect none of this,

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.563
especially Juliet, thank you, much love.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:25.533
I appreciate it.

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:27.880
You know, it helps a whole lot.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.210
I can get shoes now.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.043
- [Interviewer] Yeah, no,

00:07:30.043 --> 00:07:30.876
but it must make you feel good too,

00:07:30.876 --> 00:07:32.800
that somebody cares out there, right?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.370
- Yes, it's so scary.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:37.983
It's like seriously, because
I didn't expect none of this.

00:07:37.983 --> 00:07:38.816
None of it.

00:07:38.816 --> 00:07:41.420
And I'm like, really just appreciative.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:42.963
- [Interviewer] Have you
shared this story with anybody?

00:07:42.963 --> 00:07:43.796
Like on set?

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.493
- No I haven't even seen it myself.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.232
No I was totally embarrassed--

00:07:48.232 --> 00:07:49.320
- [Interviewer] With
your friends and stuff.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.270
You don't really?

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.410
- No, I walked up on a friend of mine,

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.203
she said I'm looking at
your story right now,

00:07:54.203 --> 00:07:55.690
I said, no, don't do that.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:56.523
Don't look at it.

00:07:56.523 --> 00:07:57.356
You know?

00:07:57.356 --> 00:07:58.500
And she was like, it's okay.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.580
I was like, no, you know,
no, I haven't looked at it.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.413
- [Interviewer] To go through this

00:08:03.413 --> 00:08:05.630
because there's shame involved too, right?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.463
- A lot.

00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:09.669
- [Interviewer] I mean you're
not to blame for it, but--

00:08:09.669 --> 00:08:11.570
- We all go through a lot.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:14.250
But a lot of things I've been through

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.810
is just hard to talk
about and tell about it.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:20.080
And people close to me and
people, you know what I'm saying?

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.460
That I share, you know, a life with,

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.030
for the streets and everything.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:25.863
'Cause people in the streets

00:08:25.863 --> 00:08:28.410
we're all street family we're really

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.290
like family because we all out here

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.170
in the streets going
through the same thing.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.710
So we have nobody to depend
on other than ourselves.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.430
And we kind of like
look out for each other.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.623
Like my special friend that, you know,

00:08:39.623 --> 00:08:43.160
came to me and told me that about the,

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.460
you know, situation, the donation.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.160
I was like, seriously.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.810
I was like, oh my God, I can't believe it.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.540
You know, I really can't believe it.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.500
I want to thank everybody.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.493
That cares 'cause no one really cared.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:56.923
You know?

00:08:56.923 --> 00:08:57.756
No one really cares

00:08:57.756 --> 00:08:59.580
about what happens to
us out on the street.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.860
They look at us like,
oh, there's this whores.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.450
They're just out there
doing this and doing that.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:08.450
But it's not that we go
through a lot, a whole lot.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.250
And we only have each other to be family

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.270
we have real family, yeah,

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.330
but most of the time

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.460
they're not understanding to
what we go through out here.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:25.080
So we depend on each other for
moral support and everything.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.190
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.190
And like I said once again,

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.970
I want to thank everybody,

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.630
you know, for caring mostly, you know,

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.650
and I appreciate their
donations and everything.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.620
And thank you Juliet, once again.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:38.280
I'm really nervous right now

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.727
because this is just such a shock to me

00:09:40.727 --> 00:09:44.310
but I wasn't expecting none of this.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.180
- [Interviewer] I'm glad,
you look happy and healthy.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.213
- [Ann] I've been trying,
I been sleeping a lot.

00:09:49.213 --> 00:09:50.680
- [Interviewer] Last time you
looked much more stressed.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.070
- [Ann] Well, yeah, yeah.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.630
I was way way stressed as I
think that's why I'm afraid to

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.630
look at my own interview.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.763
I haven't seen it.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.250
I didn't know anything about the comments

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.083
- [Interviewer] Does
it keep you up at night

00:10:01.083 --> 00:10:02.817
or anything like that?

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:09.270
- [Ann] A lot of times, you
know, I sleep periodically.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:14.800
It's like, if I sit still
longer than a minute or two,

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.257
I'm asleep, you know,

00:10:17.257 --> 00:10:19.640
'cause I really don't sleep well.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:24.640
I have nightmares, you know,
sometimes it's hard for me.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:26.820
I've went into this.

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:31.820
Like I've always had depression
thing, but I now it's like,

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.180
it's trying to overwhelm me and take

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.760
over and I'm really fighting it right now.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.593
You know?

00:10:36.593 --> 00:10:38.260
'Cause sometimes it's hard
for me to just open the door

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:41.470
and go outside, go across
the street to the store.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.450
It's just really hard, you know?

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:48.170
And I'm dealing with it.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.300
But I mean, maybe I don't
know I need counseling,

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:55.060
and you know, a little bit more help.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.840
I'm not talking about financially.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:00.253
I'm talking about mentally
and stuff like that.

00:11:00.253 --> 00:11:02.916
Because this tends to take
a toll on you, you know.

00:11:02.916 --> 00:11:04.713
- [Interviewer] You're very strong.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:07.150
- [Ann] No I'm not.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:08.820
